Now the RearrangeService — the core shift logic. Let me write it.

Key logic:
- `evaluateShift(DayPlan plan, List<Occupancy> occupancies)` returns `ShiftResult(List<Occupancy> occupancies, List<RearrangeRecord> records, boolean shifted)`. Records built with createdAt placeholder (set at persist time... I'll pass nowMillis when building). Let me pass nowMillis into evaluateShift.

- Started check: min startUtc <= clock.instant() → unchanged.

- Loop with MIN_INTERVAL_MINUTES=5, MAX_SHIFTS=288.

- Op-day check inside loop: opDayEnd = plan.opDate().plusDays(1) atStartOfDay(OPERATION_ZONE). If any shifted occupancy endUtc > opDayEnd → 422 SHIFT_EXCEEDS_OPERATION_DAY with details: sectionId, trainNo, seq, shiftedEndUtc, operationDayEndUtc, excessMinutes.

Details maps for errors need actual/required values.

- Build records: for each original occupancy, for each active restriction overlapping the ORIGINAL occupancy on same section → record with affectedMinutes = overlap minutes of original occupancy vs restriction window. Note: violations computed on original times (the trigger). shiftedStart/End = original + totalShift.

Wait — should records be per original violation only, or also violations encountered at intermediate shifts? The record fixes "原计划时刻与新计划时刻" — original vs final shifted. Violations that triggered = those on original times. I'll record per (original occupancy, restriction overlapping original occupancy).

ShiftResult record: `List<Occupancy> occupancies, List<RearrangeRecord> records` — shifted = !records.isEmpty()... Actually shifted iff shiftMinutes > 0. records non-empty iff violations existed on original. If violations existed, shift happened (loop runs until clear, shift>0). So records non-empty ⟺ shifted. Good.

Also need to handle: what if occupancy list is empty? Plans always have ≥1 occupancy (validation). Fine.

Effective speed for record: the restriction's own maxSpeedKmh (snapshot). The "以最低速度为准" applies in diagnostics (effective speed endpoint) and conceptually; each violating restriction gets its own record.

Now RestrictionService: register/amend/revoke/get/list/effective. Uses idempotency (op types RST_CREATE, RST_AMEND, RST_REVOKE), acquires publish lock inside tx for serialization.

Hash computations:
- register: "RST_CREATE\n" + restrictionKey + sectionId + start + end + speed + operator
- amend: "RST_AMEND\n" + key + expectedVersion + sectionId + start + end + speed + operator
